WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:02.635
-Our next guests are
the Emmy-nominated creators,

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:04.003
writers, and stars
of the critically acclaimed

00:00:04.003 --> 00:00:05.271
series "PEN15."

00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:07.440
The show's final episodes
are streaming on Hulu.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.441
Let's take a look.

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:10.643
-Oh, no.
This is why I got braces.

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:11.877
Are you kidding me?

00:00:11.877 --> 00:00:14.347
-I mean, honestly,
I like you better that way.

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:15.482
-With a snaggle?

00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:17.716
I'm gonna have
to get my braces back on.

00:00:17.716 --> 00:00:20.453
-You still there?
-Hi, yeah.

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:22.688
-Turn on the radio to HOT 106.7.

00:00:22.688 --> 00:00:25.792
-Wha-- Okay.
Um, Anna.

00:00:25.792 --> 00:00:27.093
Anna, he just said
put the radio on.

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:29.328
Put it on, on 106.7.

00:00:29.328 --> 00:00:31.664
Did he get you concert tickets?
-I don't know.

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:32.932
-Please welcome back to the show

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:35.201
our friends
Anna Konkle and Maya Erskine.

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:37.203
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:47.213 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:52.085 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:52.085 --> 00:00:54.454
Welcome back, you guys!
-Thank you!

00:00:54.454 --> 00:00:57.724
-Congratulations on the show.
-And I also want to say

00:00:57.724 --> 00:00:59.692
congratulations on the fact
that you both had babies

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:01.461
in this past year.
-Thank you.

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:03.796
-Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:03.796 --> 00:01:06.532
-I would imagine --
I'm already insanely jealous

00:01:06.532 --> 00:01:07.499
of the fact
that you're best friends

00:01:07.499 --> 00:01:08.868
who co-created a show together.

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:11.170
It must have been really nice
to have kids

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:14.474
within two months of each other.
Was that a fun time?

00:01:14.474 --> 00:01:16.408
I mean, I know
it's not necessarily a fun time,

00:01:16.408 --> 00:01:17.910
but was it made more fun?

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:19.879
-Up all night, never sleeping.

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:23.549
-Haven't slept for eight months,
but, yeah, it's been great.

00:01:23.549 --> 00:01:25.451
It's been so helpful to have
each other go through it,

00:01:25.451 --> 00:01:27.920
'cause it's so hard.
-It was weird

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:30.756
learning about lactating,
in general.

00:01:30.756 --> 00:01:32.859
-Uh-huh.
-And at home during COVID,

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:35.227
'cause I didn't have
to deal with going out

00:01:35.227 --> 00:01:38.697
and learning about,
like, pads and the bras.

00:01:38.697 --> 00:01:40.032
I'm sure you really want
to talk about this.

00:01:40.032 --> 00:01:43.369
-Well, no, I mean, I think,
having gone through it,

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:45.671
the body does not know
that you're out in public.

00:01:45.671 --> 00:01:48.307
-It does not.
I have learned.

00:01:48.307 --> 00:01:51.211
And, actually, I think I told --
We were out to dinner,

00:01:51.211 --> 00:01:52.579
and it was one of
the first dinners out.

00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:53.846
I was feeling like a human being

00:01:53.846 --> 00:01:55.647
with our daughter
and my partner.

00:01:55.647 --> 00:01:57.684
And I'm feeling good about
myself, and we're leaving,

00:01:57.684 --> 00:02:00.653
and Aaron Paul is there,
and he starts talking to us

00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:03.689
about our daughter,
and he was really, really sweet.

00:02:03.689 --> 00:02:05.758
I'm like, "Yeah, we're having
a great time here."

00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:09.561
And we leave, and I realize
that my white shirt

00:02:09.561 --> 00:02:14.934
has fully wet spot
and my nipple is just there.

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:17.003
[ Laughter ]
Humiliating.

00:02:17.003 --> 00:02:19.138
Humiliating.
-Well, I'm wondering

00:02:19.138 --> 00:02:22.341
why Aaron Paul was trying so
hard to extend the conversation.

00:02:22.341 --> 00:02:23.943
-Oh, God!
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:26.079
-I'm sorry, Aaron Paul.
I'm sorry.

00:02:26.079 --> 00:02:31.116
-So, the brilliant conceit
of this show is you, as adults,

00:02:31.116 --> 00:02:33.286
have been playing yourselves
as 13-year-olds.

00:02:33.286 --> 00:02:35.654
Now that you have children,
have you thought about the fact

00:02:35.654 --> 00:02:39.658
that this might be a document
to one day show them?

00:02:39.658 --> 00:02:42.495
-I really don't think my son's
gonna want to watch this,

00:02:42.495 --> 00:02:44.330
especially 'cause there
are episodes of me

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:46.332
doing things like --
-Masturbating.

00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:47.666
-Masturbating.
Thank you, Anna.

00:02:47.666 --> 00:02:50.536
[ Laughter ]
And I don't know if I can say --

00:02:50.536 --> 00:02:52.571
I don't want to give away,
but there are other bases

00:02:52.571 --> 00:02:55.174
that I get to past kissing.
-Yeah.

00:02:55.174 --> 00:02:56.542
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.542 --> 00:02:58.944
-I don't want him to see that,
but I think it could be

00:02:58.944 --> 00:03:01.013
a good conversation starter,
maybe, you know?

00:03:01.013 --> 00:03:02.281
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:03:02.281 --> 00:03:04.082
I do think it's interesting
because it's like --

00:03:04.082 --> 00:03:06.352
it would be totally fine for,
like, a mom to explain

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:07.753
to her son
about masturbating

00:03:07.753 --> 00:03:09.555
but probably best not to, like,
"Let me show you."

00:03:09.555 --> 00:03:12.792
-"Let me show you how I did it
at your age."

00:03:12.792 --> 00:03:14.026
-Yeah, "And don't worry.

00:03:14.026 --> 00:03:15.527
A lot of people
have seen your mom doing this.

00:03:15.527 --> 00:03:17.329
Don't worry.
This was on TV."

00:03:17.329 --> 00:03:19.999
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.999 --> 00:03:22.802
-Oh, my God.
-You guys always borrow

00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:25.004
from your regular life
and your experience

00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:26.472
and your history
and things you remember

00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:29.008
about being
that really awkward age.

00:03:29.008 --> 00:03:32.712
I always am desperate
to know what, from the show,

00:03:32.712 --> 00:03:36.181
in recent seasons
is true to your life.

00:03:36.181 --> 00:03:39.718
-I mean, I would say
like 80% is probably true.

00:03:39.718 --> 00:03:42.688
There's something this season
where Maya gets, like,

00:03:42.688 --> 00:03:44.223
yellow-tinted glasses.
-Here.

00:03:44.223 --> 00:03:46.758
We have a photo
of the yellow-tint glasses.

00:03:46.758 --> 00:03:48.494
-Very hot.
-Which look really cool,

00:03:48.494 --> 00:03:52.198
but, actually, I was diagnosed

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:53.899
with what's called
Irlen Syndrome.

00:03:53.899 --> 00:03:55.968
I don't know if any of you
have it here.

00:03:55.968 --> 00:03:58.971
But it basically --
First, I was told I have ADD,

00:03:58.971 --> 00:04:02.441
so, you know, the doctor gave me
a prescription for Ritalin,

00:04:02.441 --> 00:04:04.977
and then he was like,
"You get extended time

00:04:04.977 --> 00:04:07.814
on testing for SATs,"
and I was like, "Great.

00:04:07.814 --> 00:04:09.281
I definitely have ADD."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:09.281 --> 00:04:10.450
And then he was like,

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:13.019
"How do you feel about
fluorescent lights?"

00:04:13.019 --> 00:04:16.856
And I was like, "I don't feel
good about -- I don't like them.

00:04:16.856 --> 00:04:18.891
They don't feel good.
Why? Why?"

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:21.127
And he's like,
"Because these glasses.

00:04:21.127 --> 00:04:24.296
Like, these glasses
will help you focus better,

00:04:24.296 --> 00:04:26.899
and you can learn better."

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:30.636
And I wasn't that convinced
because they were those,

00:04:30.636 --> 00:04:33.139
and, basically,
he showed me a picture

00:04:33.139 --> 00:04:35.874
of Haley Joel Osment
on the red carpet wearing, like,

00:04:35.874 --> 00:04:37.476
yellow-tinted glasses,
and he was like,

00:04:37.476 --> 00:04:40.679
"He has Irlen Syndrome,
and so you should wear them."

00:04:40.679 --> 00:04:42.849
So I did.
Fast-forward --

00:04:42.849 --> 00:04:46.152
That convinced me.
We're friends now.

00:04:46.152 --> 00:04:47.387
-You and Haley?
-Yeah, he was like,

00:04:47.387 --> 00:04:48.687
"I never had Irlen Syndrome.

00:04:48.687 --> 00:04:52.358
That was just me
on the red carpet.

00:04:52.358 --> 00:04:54.360
-That was fashion.
-Yeah. That was fashion.

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:56.062
Yeah.
-I like that you thought

00:04:56.062 --> 00:04:58.197
that diagnosis was exciting
to you because --

00:04:58.197 --> 00:05:00.232
-It was, yeah.
-But you were excited

00:05:00.232 --> 00:05:02.368
about getting braces.
-Yeah.

00:05:02.368 --> 00:05:04.804
-In real life.
-Yes, in fifth grade.

00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:07.340
Fourth grade, actually,
I knew I was gonna have

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:09.542
to get braces
'cause my teeth were crazy.

00:05:09.542 --> 00:05:12.478
And so, yeah, my orthodontist
said, "Okay.

00:05:12.478 --> 00:05:14.313
We could do it now,"
and I had them for two years.

00:05:14.313 --> 00:05:17.749
I got them off, and then
one tooth just went rogue.

00:05:17.749 --> 00:05:19.985
-Uh-huh.
-And I also had that

00:05:19.985 --> 00:05:22.754
appliance thing that, like,
expanded the top of your --

00:05:22.754 --> 00:05:24.323
How is that legal?
-Yeah.

00:05:24.323 --> 00:05:26.625
-Yeah.
-That hurt.

00:05:26.625 --> 00:05:28.494
And so, yeah.
So then I got the braces off,

00:05:28.494 --> 00:05:30.496
and the tooth came off --
I mean, out.

00:05:30.496 --> 00:05:32.965
Basically off.
And wearing the retainer

00:05:32.965 --> 00:05:34.967
didn't work,
and so eventually --

00:05:34.967 --> 00:05:37.202
Actually, my orthodontist died.
[ Audience groans ]

00:05:37.202 --> 00:05:38.437
I know.
-Yeah.

00:05:38.437 --> 00:05:41.740
[ Laughter ]
But again...

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:43.476
He wasn't maybe
great at his job.

00:05:43.476 --> 00:05:46.712
[ Laughter ]

00:05:46.712 --> 00:05:48.147
Just saying.
Rest in peace.

00:05:48.147 --> 00:05:50.282
-I'm crying. I'm crying.
-Yeah.

00:05:50.282 --> 00:05:53.152
-No.
And then the new orthodontist

00:05:53.152 --> 00:05:56.121
was like, "You messed up."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:56.121 --> 00:05:58.624
And then said, "You need braces
for another two years."

00:05:58.624 --> 00:06:00.727
-Really?
So you got them back on.

00:06:00.727 --> 00:06:04.229
I mean, I had braces for maybe
five years, start to finish,

00:06:04.229 --> 00:06:06.332
but at least I never had
that moment where they came off

00:06:06.332 --> 00:06:07.900
and I thought
I was out of the woods.

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:10.002
-Right.
-That's really hard.

00:06:10.002 --> 00:06:11.704
-That's dark.
-But five years is a long time.

00:06:11.704 --> 00:06:13.772
-Yeah, mine were --
mine were rough.

00:06:13.772 --> 00:06:16.042
I think we just
forgot to go back.

00:06:16.042 --> 00:06:17.843
-Right.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:17.843 --> 00:06:19.711
-I think one day, like,
we just got super used to them,

00:06:19.711 --> 00:06:21.647
and then, one day,
my dad was like, "Hold on."

00:06:21.647 --> 00:06:23.416
[ Laughter ]

00:06:23.416 --> 00:06:24.584
"You're about to go to college."

00:06:24.584 --> 00:06:28.354
Hey, you guys write a lot
about your relationships

00:06:28.354 --> 00:06:31.824
with your mother --
your mothers this season.

00:06:31.824 --> 00:06:34.226
Your mother -- Your actual
mother plays your mother.

00:06:34.226 --> 00:06:36.495
-She does.
-Immediate star.

00:06:36.495 --> 00:06:39.632
Is she aware?
-Oh, she's aware, yeah.

00:06:39.632 --> 00:06:41.834
-Yeah.
-She's taking interviews,

00:06:41.834 --> 00:06:44.904
she's doing, you know --
she's getting other auditions.

00:06:44.904 --> 00:06:47.640
She's using my agents.
I think they're hers now.

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:49.108
I'm not sure.
But, yeah, she's great.

00:06:49.108 --> 00:06:51.210
-What would she be like
if she had joined us

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:52.678
on the couch today?

00:06:52.678 --> 00:06:55.181
-Oh, yeah, she should be here.
-I know.

00:06:55.181 --> 00:06:57.616
She would roast me.
She would definitely burn me

00:06:57.616 --> 00:06:59.451
if she was sitting
right next to me.

00:06:59.451 --> 00:07:03.121
I don't think it would be --
-Like, soft burns?

00:07:03.121 --> 00:07:06.525
-The thing is, she's Japanese,
so it's just very much

00:07:06.525 --> 00:07:09.728
part of that culture to, like,
downplay everything.

00:07:09.728 --> 00:07:11.630
Like, "Don't look
at my daughter, please.

00:07:11.630 --> 00:07:13.465
Like, she has short legs.
Like, don't look at her."

00:07:13.465 --> 00:07:17.669
You know, like, it's very --
That has happened.

00:07:17.669 --> 00:07:19.839
-I love your legs.
-But she says it's, like,

00:07:19.839 --> 00:07:21.607
a false modesty
'cause she actually feels

00:07:21.607 --> 00:07:24.643
very proud about her daughter,
but she doesn't want to, like,

00:07:24.643 --> 00:07:26.245
say that out loud to everyone.

00:07:26.245 --> 00:07:27.613
She doesn't want it
to seem too perfect.

00:07:27.613 --> 00:07:30.983
-I like that your mom and you,
I guess, to some degree,

00:07:30.983 --> 00:07:35.053
almost fell for or did fall for
a scam modeling agency?

00:07:35.053 --> 00:07:38.190
-Yeah, yeah.
Yeah, because we lived

00:07:38.190 --> 00:07:40.326
outside of Boston
in a little suburb,

00:07:40.326 --> 00:07:42.494
and so the dream was,
you go in the city,

00:07:42.494 --> 00:07:44.029
and you're gonna be discovered.

00:07:44.029 --> 00:07:46.866
And I thought that happened
in Boston.

00:07:46.866 --> 00:07:48.734
Someone stopped me.
I'm 5'8",

00:07:48.734 --> 00:07:51.704
so I think that was
the only reason in retrospect.

00:07:51.704 --> 00:07:54.073
And they were like,
"Are you a model?"

00:07:54.073 --> 00:07:56.342
Clearly not a model.

00:07:56.342 --> 00:07:58.110
And I was like,
"No, but I could be."

00:07:58.110 --> 00:07:59.511
-They were like,
"You look like --

00:07:59.511 --> 00:08:00.646
We don't say this all the time.

00:08:00.646 --> 00:08:02.548
You look like
you've had braces twice."

00:08:02.548 --> 00:08:03.682
[ Laughter ]

00:08:03.682 --> 00:08:05.484
"That's how good
your teeth are."

00:08:05.484 --> 00:08:08.854
-Yes. Yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:08.854 --> 00:08:12.524
And this woman gave me a card,

00:08:12.524 --> 00:08:15.327
and I went to a hotel room --
with my mom --

00:08:15.327 --> 00:08:17.696
-Okay.
-Maybe a month later.

00:08:17.696 --> 00:08:20.299
-I mean, in this day and age,
that's a huge -- yeah.

00:08:20.299 --> 00:08:22.301
-Yeah, yeah.
No.

00:08:22.301 --> 00:08:23.970
And, yeah, they were like,

00:08:23.970 --> 00:08:26.672
"It's gonna be $7,000
for you to model.

00:08:26.672 --> 00:08:30.309
We have to get pictures,"
and my mom was sold.

00:08:30.309 --> 00:08:32.578
And I was --
I actually ended up being like,

00:08:32.578 --> 00:08:34.413
"I don't --
That doesn't feel right."

00:08:34.413 --> 00:08:35.547
-Your mom was sold.

00:08:35.547 --> 00:08:37.082
-And she was like,
"We have to do this."

00:08:37.082 --> 00:08:39.785
Meanwhile, I'm getting,
you know, consignment clothes.

00:08:39.785 --> 00:08:41.754
But for some reason, she's like,
"Let's just spend it."

00:08:41.754 --> 00:08:42.888
[ Laughter ]

00:08:42.888 --> 00:08:44.323
-That's crazy.
-"Just do it."

00:08:44.323 --> 00:08:48.594
It's really sweet, actually.
-You guys, I think, people --

00:08:48.594 --> 00:08:50.295
it's safe to say
a lot of people are heartbroken

00:08:50.295 --> 00:08:52.231
that you're closing this
thing up after three chapters,

00:08:52.231 --> 00:08:54.433
but that was always your plan.
-Mm-hmm.

00:08:54.433 --> 00:08:58.637
-Are you satisfied
with how it's all ending?

00:08:58.637 --> 00:09:00.906
-I feel -- Yeah.
I feel really good about it.

00:09:00.906 --> 00:09:04.743
I feel happy where we left
Maya and Anna's characters,

00:09:04.743 --> 00:09:07.145
but it is sad, you know?
-It's bittersweet.

00:09:07.145 --> 00:09:08.680
-Yeah.
-Well, congratulations.

00:09:08.680 --> 00:09:12.585
It's such a beautiful, deeply
funny show, and it's so unique,

00:09:12.585 --> 00:09:13.786
as unique as anything on TV.

00:09:13.786 --> 00:09:15.788
So, thank you
for three incredible chapters.

00:09:15.788 --> 00:09:18.456
You guys,
Anna Konkle, Maya Erskine.

00:09:18.456 --> 00:09:21.027
The final episodes of "PEN15"
are streaming on Hulu.

